document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded',()=>setTimeout(()=>{const h=document.querySelector('#bi-analogue');if(!h||document.querySelector('#stream-b'))return;const r='balanced-imitation-20261019/streamB/',s=document.createElement('details');s.id='stream-b';s.innerHTML=`<summary>Stream B: pair-conditioned family means</summary><p class="origin-line">Origin: New analysis (exploratory)</p><p>Stream A uses one shared family embedding. Stream B jointly embeds and clusters each biological tutor–pupil pair; its tutor endpoint is a pair-conditioned mean, not an intrinsic tutor statistic. Pair categories are not homologous, so only entropies are compared.</p><p>45 completed pairs; 26 tutors (9 with ≥2 pairs); original and PCA75 arms; inclusive and assigned-only treatments. Sampling-noise reliability is 0.98 at τ=10, but pair-partition instability is not covered by the null.</p>${['fig_B1_tutor_vs_meanpupil.png','fig_B2_pair_level.png','fig_B3_null.png'].map((p,i)=>`<figure><img loading="lazy" src="${r+p}" alt="Stream B figure ${i+1}"><figcaption>Stream B${i+1}. <a download href="${r+p}">Download</a></figcaption></figure>`).join('')}<div class="how-to-read"><strong>What we expect / Why / What it does not show.</strong> A slope below 1 and positive contrast are consistent with regression toward a common level. The contrast is large in all four settings, but slopes depend on representation (0.49 original; 0.06 PCA75) and include zero in three of four. This does not show causes, equivalence with the paper’s entropy, or agreement of Streams A and B.</div><p><a download href="${r}streamB_summary.csv">Download summary</a> · <a download href="${r}streamB_tutor_instability.csv">Download instability table</a></p><p>Fixed-state analogue (one global partition) — planned, not run*.</p>`;h.after(s)},0));
